    {
      "title": "Refault cost: major faults and reads against the throttle",
      "description": "Where evicted file pages come back to bite. WiredTiger reads data files with pread, not mmap, so pages the kernel reclaimed return as ordinary read() I/O - watch 'device reads' against the dashed line, which is the probe's configured blkio cap (8 MiB/s in compose.yml, standing in for a small cloud volume; replace with the real volume's ceiling elsewhere). Reads pinned on that line mean every further miss queues behind the throttle and surfaces as query latency. Major faults stay near zero for mongod and matter mainly for mmap-based engines; cAdvisor has no workingset_refault_file, so read() volume is the refault-cost signal here. 'WT pages into cache' is the same demand counted from Mongo's side.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "PBFA97CFB590B2093"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(container_memory_failures_total{failure_type=\"pgmajfault\",scope=\"container\",name=~\"$container\"}[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "major faults/s",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "rate(container_fs_reads_bytes_total{name=~\"$container\"}[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "device reads B/s",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "rate(pages_read_into_cache{instance=~\"$instance\"}[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "WT pages into cache/s",
          "refId": "C"
        },
        {
          "expr": "8388608 + 0 * container_spec_memory_limit_bytes{name=~\"$container\"}",
          "legendFormat": "blkio read throttle (8 MiB/s)",
          "refId": "D"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "device reads B/s"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "Bps"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "blkio read throttle (8 MiB/s)"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "Bps"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.fillOpacity",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    10,
                    10
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "PSI: fraction of time stalled",
      "description": "Linux pressure-stall information for the mongo cgroup, plotted as seconds stalled per second (0 to 1). 'some' means at least one task was blocked on memory or I/O during the interval; 'full' means all of them were. The memory panels explain the mechanism; this one measures how much time it actually costs.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "PBFA97CFB590B2093"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(container_pressure_memory_waiting_seconds_total{name=~\"$container\"}[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "memory some",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "rate(container_pressure_memory_stalled_seconds_total{name=~\"$container\"}[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "memory full",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "rate(container_pressure_io_waiting_seconds_total{name=~\"$container\"}[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "io some",
          "refId": "C"
        },
        {
          "expr": "rate(container_pressure_io_stalled_seconds_total{name=~\"$container\"}[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "io full",
          "refId": "D"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 15
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "WT occupancy vs cgroup usage, same 0-100 axis",
      "description": "Two utilization views of the same container. WT occupancy is measured against the WT cache maximum and can sit comfortably under 80% while the container's working set is pinned at memory.max. When the two lines diverge - occupancy moderate, working set near 100 - the shortage is in the cgroup's file cache, not inside WiredTiger, and WT-level metrics alone will not show it. The third line tracks how much of the limit is still file cache. With no container limit the two %-of-limit lines go empty rather than reporting against a meaningless number, and a %-of-host-RAM line appears instead.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "PBFA97CFB590B2093"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "mongodb_wiredtiger_cache_occupancy_ratio{instance=~\"$instance\"} * 100",
          "legendFormat": "WT occupancy % of WT max",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "container_memory_working_set_bytes{name=~\"$container\"} / (container_spec_memory_limit_bytes{name=~\"$container\"} > 0) * 100",
          "legendFormat": "working set % of memory.max",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "container_memory_cache{name=~\"$container\"} / (container_spec_memory_limit_bytes{name=~\"$container\"} > 0) * 100",
          "legendFormat": "file cache % of memory.max",
          "refId": "C"
        },
        {
          "expr": "container_memory_working_set_bytes{name=~\"$container\"} / on() group_left() node_memory_MemTotal_bytes{machine=~\"$machine\"} * 100 unless on() (container_spec_memory_limit_bytes{name=~\"$container\"} > 0)",
          "legendFormat": "working set % of host RAM (no limit set)",
          "refId": "D"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "line"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Ceiling events: memory.max hits and swap",
      "description": "failcnt counts allocation attempts that hit memory.max. A sustained rate with swap flat means the kernel is absorbing those hits through reclaim; the PSI and refault panels show what that costs. Swap growing means overflow is being written out instead. An OOM kill in memory.events is the end state: anonymous memory could not be reclaimed and the process was killed.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 18
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "PBFA97CFB590B2093"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(container_memory_failcnt{name=~\"$container\"}[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "memory.max hits/s",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "container_memory_swap{name=~\"$container\"}",
          "legendFormat": "swap bytes",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "swap bytes"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "bytes"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
