        "content": "## Captured load windows\n\n**2026-08-24 - escalating Celery read load, 100/200/400 tasks per s**\nDriver ran 19:23:22Z-19:32:19Z against the probe mongo (640 MiB limit,\n256 MiB WT cache, 1.1 GB data, 8 MiB/s read throttle). Observed: anon\n+63 MiB, file cache -24 MiB (inactive band), reads pinned at the\nthrottle, PSI io-some 81%, ticket pool saturated (7-8 of 8 out,\n6.5k-task backlog). Memory squeeze reached the cheap-reclaim stage;\nactive file was not yet cut - a longer run goes further.\n\n[Replay: before / during / after (19:08-19:48Z)](/d/xycalc-wt-cgroup?from=1787598480000&to=1787600880000&var-container=xycalc-celery-probe-mongo-1)\n| [load window only](/d/xycalc-wt-cgroup?from=1787599380000&to=1787599980000&var-container=xycalc-celery-probe-mongo-1)\n\nReproduce (on the host running the probe):\n```\ncd tools/bench/celery_probe\ndocker compose --profile driver run --rm --no-deps \\\n  -e PROBE_RATES=100,200,400 -e PROBE_SECONDS=120 driver\n```\nAdd the new window here with its from/to epoch-ms so the replay list\nstays with the board.\n"
